>> title: Hungarian Goulash, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, paprika, hungarian, one-pot, stew, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: hungarian-goulash
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: gulyás, gulyas, beef goulash, slow cooker goulash, crockpot hungarian goulash
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the paprika has about thirty seconds off the heat before it scorches, and scorched paprika is bitter for the whole eight hours that follow; nothing later in the day takes it back out
>> step.2: render the onions 25 min, deep golden
>> step.3: bloom the paprika off the heat, stir the beef in
>> step.4: stew on low, 8 hr
>> step.5: reduce on high, lid off

Written for low, eight hours. Two pounds of onions cooked to deep gold is the base of a gulyás and it is twenty-five minutes of a person at a pan — the machine cannot do it, cannot start it, and cannot rescue a pot where it was skipped. What the machine does is the eight hours after. Stock halves, to two cups, and the potatoes go in at the start and come out soft-edged, which thickens it and is not a fault here.

Render @lard{2%Tbs}, @yellow onions{2%lb}(900 g; thinly sliced) in a heavy #skillet{} for ~render{25%min}, until deep golden and reduced to a quarter of their volume.

Bloom @Hungarian sweet paprika{1/4%cup}(30 g), @caraway seed{1%tsp}, @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) in @&(~1)onions{} off the heat, then stir in @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1-in cubes), @kosher salt{1%Tbs} to coat every cube.

Slow cook @&(~1)paprika base{} with @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @tomato{1%large}(chopped), @green pepper{1}(chopped), @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 2-in chunks) in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on.

Reduce @&(~1)goulash{} on high with the lid off for ~reduce{20%min}, until it is a thick soup rather than a thin one — a gulyás should coat the back of the spoon it is eaten with.
